---
import SiteLayout from "../../../../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../../../../../../components/Eyebrow.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Module 10: Basic Router Configuration — fred.fish" description="Build a router configuration from initial hostname and security settings through interface addressing, default routing, and connectivity verification." active="cisco">
<section class="source-lesson">
<div class="lesson-nav"><a href="/cisco/learning/semester-1/">← Semester 1 course</a><a href="/cisco/practice/">Adaptive practice ↗</a></div>
<header class="lesson-hero"><Eyebrow index="S1 / 10" label="MODULE 10 / ROUTER IOS CONFIGURATION" /><h1>Configure the router.<br /><span>Verify the path.</span></h1><p>Build a router configuration from initial hostname and security settings through interface addressing, default routing, and connectivity verification.</p></header>
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="lesson-number">01</div><div><h2>Establish a safe baseline</h2><p>Set a meaningful hostname, protect privileged EXEC access with enable secret, configure console and VTY access, and display an appropriate message-of-the-day banner. Use local user accounts and secure remote management such as SSH rather than exposing plaintext passwords or insecure remote access.</p><div class="lesson-source"><span>SOURCE IMAGES</span><code>IMG-0692 · IMG-0698</code></div></div></section>
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="lesson-number">02</div><div><h2>Configure routed interfaces</h2><p>Enter interface configuration mode for each required router interface. Apply an IPv4 address and subnet mask, add a useful description, and issue no shutdown when the interface should be enabled. A router interface must be correctly addressed and operational before it can route traffic for that network.</p><div class="lesson-source"><span>SOURCE IMAGES</span><code>IMG-0713 · IMG-0720</code></div></div></section>
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="lesson-number">03</div><div><h2>Configure and verify routing</h2><p>Hosts use the router interface on their own subnet as the default gateway. Routers need routes to remote networks, which may be directly connected, statically configured, or learned through a routing protocol. Use show ip interface brief, show ip route, and ping to verify interface and path state.</p><div class="lesson-source"><span>SOURCE IMAGES</span><code>IMG-0692 · IMG-0738</code></div></div></section>
<section class="lesson-end"><div><Eyebrow label="CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING" /><h2>Basic Router Configuration</h2><p>Practice the key terms, procedures, and troubleshooting decisions from this module.</p></div><a href="/cisco/practice/">Start practice →</a></section>
</section>
</SiteLayout>
